  <label>Data Science Discovery</label>
  <description>Data Science Discovery is the intersection of statistics, computation, and real-world relevance. As a project-driven course, students perform hands-on-analysis of real-world datasets to analyze and discover the impact of the data. Throughout each experience, students reflect on the social issues surrounding data analysis such as privacy and design. Proficiency exams will be offered at the beginning of each Spring and Fall semester. Same as CS 107 and IS 107.</description>
  <creditHours>4 hours.</creditHours>
  <courseSectionInformation>Proficiency exams will be offered at the beginning of each Spring and Fall semester. Same as CS 107 and IS 107.</courseSectionInformation>
  <sectionDegreeAttributes>Quantitative Reasoning I course.</sectionDegreeAttributes>
